OL,3,AWhy doomsday warnings are not the only
OL,4,Athreat to the AI juggernaut
OL,5,
OL,6,FTheir computations, which are in effect
OL,7,Fthe switching on and off of microscopic
OL,8,Fsilicon transistors that make up a
OL,9,Fchip, are actually silent. But, as with
OL,10,Fall computers, almost every watt of the
OL,11,Fsignificant electricity powering this
OL,12,Fprocess leaves as heat, and the sound
OL,13,Fyou can hear is the slow whir of
OL,14,Fthousands of fans required to prevent
OL,15,Fthe heat from frying the racks of
OL,16,Fservers. Depending on the size of the
OL,17,Fsite, you may also hear the thrum of
OL,18,Ftransformers in substations channelling
OL,19,Felectricity.
OL,23,APub: 15-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG2/2
